        rules: {
          objective: "Capture cards to reach a target score (3 points for 3 players, 7 for 2 players) and then decide whether to continue ('Go') or end ('Stop').",
          gameplay: "1. Play a card from hand to match a card of the same month on the table.\n2. Draw a card from the deck to match another card on the table.\n3. Captured cards are placed in categories: Brights (Kwang), Animals (Yul), Ribbons (Tti), or Junk (Pi).\n4. **Go or Stop**: Once you hit the target score, if you say 'Go', you continue. Each subsequent 'Go' increases your point multiplier but risks 'Go-bak' (losing everything if another player scores).",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hwatu (Go-Stop).',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Scoring follows the game-specific point or pot rules.',
            "Winning condition: Capture cards to reach a target score (3 points for 3 players, 7 for 2 players) and then decide whether to continue ('Go') or end ('Stop').",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize capturing 'Junk' (Pi) cards early. While small, getting 10 Junk cards is the easiest way to reach your first point. Watch for opponents trying to get 'Godori'.",
          intermediate: "The 'Shake': If you have 3 of the same month in hand, 'shake' them (show them) to double your score if you win.",
          advanced: "Risk Math: Only call 'Go' if you have a clear path to your next point (e.g., you only need one more ribbon) AND you know your opponents are far from their target score.",
          tips: [
            "The 'Kwang' (Bright) cards are high reward but hard to complete.",
            "Try to 'Sswe-rip' (Sweep the table) to gain Junk cards from your opponents.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
