          deckDescription: 'The 48-card Hwatu (Korean flower card) deck, derived from Japanese Hanafuda: 12 months (suits), each with four cards (two normal and two special). Used for Go-Stop and other Korean fishing games where players capture cards to form combinations (Jokbo) and choose Go or Stop.',
          suitDescription: 'The twelve months are represented by floral motifs (January Pine through December Paulownia); each month has four cards. Cards are captured by matching the month or by forming sets; bright, animal, and ribbon cards have special scoring roles.',
          rankDescription: 'Cards within each month have different types: standard, bright (high value), animal, or ribbon. Ranking is by month and card type for capture and scoring; the same month matches, and specific combinations (Jokbo) award bonus points when declaring Go or Stop.',
          dealPattern: '',
          bettingLimits: 'NA',
